00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:20.803
- You can't hear me?

00:00:20.803 --> 00:00:21.990
- I wish, I can't hear you,

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.100
but I wish I could read lips,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:23.933
but I can't.

00:00:23.933 --> 00:00:24.766
I'll put Louie down.

00:00:24.766 --> 00:00:26.190
- Okay.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:28.143
Navy SEAL.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.460
Navy.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.310
Navy.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:32.287
- No.

00:00:32.287 --> 00:00:33.120
- SEAL.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:33.953
- This is like a game.

00:00:33.953 --> 00:00:35.675
Sounds like shirt, okay.

00:00:35.675 --> 00:00:36.678
- You play.

00:00:36.678 --> 00:00:38.750
- Yes, "SEAL Team."

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.583
- Yes!

00:00:39.583 --> 00:00:40.937
- Yes, "SEAL Team."

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.070
- Yep, that was a lot
of the interview, folks.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:47.396
So, now in honor of Aidy's
show "Shrill" on Hulu,

00:00:47.396 --> 00:00:49.660
it's time to put both our mics on mute

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.343
and play the David Boreanaz
Can't Hear Me Game.

00:00:53.296 --> 00:00:56.013
♪ The David Boreanaz Can't Hear Me Game ♪

00:00:56.013 --> 00:00:58.610
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:58.610 --> 00:00:59.759
I love you, Jessie.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:02.580
How competitive do you
get on game nights, Aidy?

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.660
Are you like all in?

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.005
- I am the opposite where
I'm like, "You win, I lose."

00:01:08.005 --> 00:01:09.240
- [Kelly] Oh, my gosh.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.034
- But today I'm gonna really go for it.

00:01:11.034 --> 00:01:14.266
- We are, we could not be more opposite,

00:01:14.266 --> 00:01:16.111
so that's fine, we're gonna be playing

00:01:16.111 --> 00:01:17.000
for the audience.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.850
We're not going against each other.

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:20.260
Just kidding.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.483
So this is a virtual version

00:01:21.483 --> 00:01:23.933
of the old 19th century game Charades.

00:01:23.933 --> 00:01:25.630
Aidy and I take turns trying

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.113
to get the other to say a word or phrase

00:01:27.113 --> 00:01:28.970
while our mics are muted.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:30.490
We're allowed to say the words,

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.577
use motions and use props.

00:01:32.577 --> 00:01:35.393
If we want to pass, we
hold up our pass card.

00:01:35.393 --> 00:01:38.440
If we can get a total
of eight words correct

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.610
in two rounds, everyone in the house seats

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:43.000
will win a prize, so, okay.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.340
Mute my mic and I'll go
first, are you ready.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:47.173
Go!

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:49.684
- Oh, ice cream.

00:01:49.684 --> 00:01:50.685
- Ice cream cone.

00:01:50.685 --> 00:01:52.290
(bell ringing)

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:53.123
